There's an internal litmus test that a lot of actors have. Maybe they'll admit it. Maybe they won't. But a part of it is when you read something and you're like, &#x201C;I don't want to see anyone else do this.&#x201D; Like, &#x201C;I feel like I have the most to add to it or bring to it, and I don't want to see anybody else's version of this. I want to do my version.&#x201D; So, that was a big deciding factor. Just reading it and being like, &#x201C;No, it's too special&#x201D; on the page; I want to be able to do it myself. These characters that mean so much, that are so impactful, it's an honor. It's like why wouldn't I want to have that you know on my belt if you will, that I got to play Carl Weathers. It's amazing! blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-articleX-uid3' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[620,366]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

His warmth was something that people don't really get to see too much. Just looking at him, he could come across as like this physically imposing, maybe scary individual, but I've spoken to people who've spent a lot of real time with him, and you know they've all said just how kind he was.

I tried to add that into the film just in terms of his relationship with Sly. When he finally admits that he's not a boxer, and the fact that they could both laugh at that moment and then bond on something like, &#x201C;Yes, we&#x2019;re adversaries in this film, but, for the purposes of making this film, we're gonna have to lock in and be able to trust each other, and it'd be nice if we liked each other too.&#x201D;

I'd be keen to know if he really understood what he would mean to the legacy of this franchise, not only in the four &#x201C;Rocky&#x201D; films he made, but, if you count the &#x201C;Creed&#x201D; films [too]. The fact that there was a whole other world that spawned off people's love for you and your character and your lineage, that we can make a whole series of movies about his son now.

That really is Carl Weathers and his legacy. Not every actor rather is going to step into that role and last for four movies and then [influence] three more after that. Like, that's because of him. So, I would wonder if he knew on those first days on &#x201C;Rocky I,&#x201D; like, did you ever think it could be this?

I was just over 200 pounds when I found out that I got this job and I found out that I had two months to get ready for this. So, my initial thought process was, &#x201C;Let me just start eating and bulking up,&#x201D; like protein for breakfast, lunch and dinner, just go ham. And I spoke to a trainer friend of mine, and he said, if you work on cutting your body fat percentage down, effectively losing weight while keeping your muscle, you'll be great. And people are gonna think you look bigger than you actually are. Trust me. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-articleX-uid4' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[620,366]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

So, that became my process: weight training at the gym in the morning; going down to Kingsway Boxing Club in Toronto with my trainer Jennifer Huggins and we just took it day by day, step by step. It started with cardio, just getting my endurance level up, then it was footwork. I didn't realize how big footwork was in boxing. Just learning how to not move around like a baby deer. And then unlearning all of those things to be the unpolished version of Apollo Creed. There were layers and levels to it. By the time I was done, I ended up dropping like 20-25 pounds and in the film, I&#x2019;m 170-175 max.

I'm still healing from some of the punches I took, but it was a lot of fun to work with Anthony and spend so much time with him. Just getting close with him, building like a bond and a level of trust with each other. That's crucial, time for character development. For us to actually be going through the motions of the choreography in that last fight scene, getting into the psychology of what it meant to be a boxer and respecting that art form, the process was equally as important as the filming itself.

First of all, I wear like the greatest suits ever, so that's really fly. They're all like custom made, so hopefully the production will give them to me afterward, because like who else are they gonna fit? So that's been really really cool.

And then, just playing this young, smart, quick-witted lawyer has been really fun. I just feel like I'm stepping outside of myself and again giving the world something that they haven't really seen me in.

Creative Arts Agency CEO Bryan Lourd urged Congress on Saturday to pass the NO FAKES Act , a bill that would regulate the wave of unauthorized AI deepfakes proliferating the internet, writing in a New York Times Opinion piece that &#x201C;every one of us should have the right to say no to an unwelcome use of our likeness.&#x201D;

The NO FAKES Act was introduced by Sen. Chris Coons (D-ME) in May, following a previous attempt at the bill last year. While it advanced out of the Senate Judiciary Committee in June and has a bipartisan coalition of co-sponsors, the full Senate has not taken it up. Lourd wrote that the bill would introduce a federal standard for &#x201C;control, consent and compensation&#x201D; surrounding deepfakes, replacing &#x201C;outdated, ill-fitting state laws, many of them written with an analog world in mind.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories ‘Unlike Anything Else’: As ‘GTA 6’ Approaches, the Gaming Industry Braces the World for Its Pop Culture Takeover ‘GTA 6’ Hits Massive $3.79 Billion in First-Day Sales

&#x201C;I come to this issue not as a policymaker but as a practitioner. I run a global talent agency. Part of our job is to help our clients license their likenesses and performances, sometimes to AI companies,&#x201D;&#xA0;he added. &#x201C;We regularly negotiate those deals, and I can tell you that the bill pending in Congress delivers what the industry needs and what will protect all Americans.&#x201D;

Lourd laid out the stakes for Hollywood by citing Tom Hanks, who warned his followers in 2023 about a dental office using an AI deepfake of a younger version of him in an advertisement. Hanks likely wouldn't have agreed to the dental ad, Lourd wrote, but he should've been given a choice before the dental office ran with an unauthorized deepfake.

&#x201C;What&#x2019;s missing is a bright-line rule affirming that right in the AI age, and it is one Congress can supply before the year is out,&#x201D;&#xA0;Lourd wrote. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

CAA has advocated against the unauthorized proliferation of celebrity deepfakes online, working with the Cate Blanchett-backed Human Consent Foundation to help people control permissions for their likenesses if they're scraped by AI models. The agency also joined the foundation and other entertainment backers in an amicus brief in the New York Times' lawsuit against OpenAI, noting the active licensing market for likenesses that's developed in the AI era.

Deepfakes have been a constant presence since large-language models emerged in 2022, with many being used to produce unauthorized and sometimes explicit depictions of actors, singers and other celebrities. Other industry backers of the NO FAKES Act include SAG-AFTRA, the Motion Picture Association, the Recording Industry Association of America, the Recording Academy and the National Association of Broadcasters, OpenAI, the AFL-CIO, YouTube and IBM.

Liz Daly Byrne , a model and philanthropist who was married to PMC vice chairman Gerry Byrne for more than 55 years, has died. She was 81.

Byrne faced a battle with cancer three years ago, and recently learned that her illness had returned. She had faced recurring complications from severe injuries suffered in a bicycle accident in 2000. Byrne died Nov. 17 after a period of home hospice care in New York. Related Stories 'Logan' Star Dafne Keen Says 'I Was Offered Cocaine' as an 11-Year-Old in Hollywood and Hugh Jackman 'Made Sure No One Abused My Hours' on Set

Byrne was active as a philanthropist and social advocate through her work with the United Nations' Operation Smile campaign, traveling internationally with the organization on medical missions. She had long been involved in causes to support military families and veterans. Byrne was remembered by her family, including her adult children, digital entrepreneur Gavin Byrne and actor Megan Byrne, as a woman who embodied &#x201C;elegance, strength, wit, faith, generosity and compassion.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Byrne was also extremely fast on her feet, as she demonstrated in 1997 during the Cannes Film Festival. During a post-screening party for Warner Bros./New Regency's buzzy period drama &#x201C;L.A. Confidential&#x201D; at a vineyard, a tipsy guest fell into the pool. As Variety reported, when Byrne saw what had happened, she &#x201C;threw off her jacket and shoes and dove into the water for a dramatic rescue, after which she calmly took her seat for the sit-down dinner at fireworks show.&#x201D;

Born in 1945, Byrne grew up in the shadow of Yankee Stadium in the Bronx. She met her future husband Gerry Byrne &#x2014; who served as publisher of Variety from 1989 to 2000 and at present is vice chair of Variety parent company PMC &#x2014; while he was attending Fordham College in the borough. The two were neighbors, but in a wonderfully Bronx love story touch, Liz Daly met Gerry Byrne one evening during a ride on the D train. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Early on, Liz Daly was drawn to New York's fashion world. She signed with top modeling agencies Mannequin and Ellen Harth and launched her career as the primary designer&#x2019;s model for top New York retailers Saks Fifth Avenue and Bonwit Teller. In addition to appearing in TV commercials, Byrne spent years as a runway model with Anne Klein, Donna Karan, Oscar de la Renta and Bill Tice. She then spent another decade worked with renowned designers Bob Mackie and Ray Aghayan.

Daly and Byrne married in 1969 at the chapel at St. Patrick's Cathedral Chapel, after Gerry Byrne completed a three-year tour with the U.S. Marine Corps in Vietnam. In tribute to her husband's service, Liz Byrne successfully launched a POW bracelet program to honor the sacrifices made by some families. The effort took root after being publicized nationally through coverage in the New York Times.

Byrne was a dedicated marathon runner who participated in multiple New York City Marathons as well as runs hosted by the Marines in Washington, D.C. She was active in numerous nonprofits and in entertainment and media industry charitable efforts.

